<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  FIXTURE PROVENANCE — an ADVERSARIAL fixture, written for this repository.

  This is NOT the vendor's documented example (that is hivemq-credentials-4.6.16.xml).
  Every user, role and permission below was written here on 2026-08-14, in the File RBAC
  extension's 4.6.16 element vocabulary, to pin three review findings:

   1. TOML ESCAPING. `<name>CORP\jdoe</name>` — an AD-style username, exactly what a
      file-RBAC or ESE population looks like — used to come out as
      `identities = ["CORP\jdoe"]`, which tomllib REJECTS ("Unescaped '\' in a string").
      A TOML parse failure is a WHOLE-DOCUMENT failure, so that single user made the
      broker refuse to load ANY of the migrated policy: the migration stalls on an opaque
      parser error instead of a TODO. The second user and one topic carry a double quote,
      the other character that has to be escaped.
   2. THE SHELL LINE MUST ALSO SURVIVE. The re-enrolment command this converter prints is
      meant to be copied and run, and the hash-password command, run unquoted, enrols a
      DIFFERENT username (the backslash escapes the j).
   3. UNKNOWN-ELEMENT HANDLING ON THE SECURITY FILE. `<enabled>false</enabled>` on a user
      and the whole `<extra-policy-section>` below are not in the 4.6.16 vocabulary. They
      used to pass in silence — on the file that IS the authorization policy — while the
      config walk reported every unknown element by path. The extension is versioned
      independently of this converter, so a newer or vendor-extended element is precisely
      the input that needs a TODO. Note the direction: a user disabled by an element this
      converter does not understand still gets allow rules, which is fail-OPEN.

  There are NO real password hashes here: the <password> values are the literal string
  "not-a-real-hash", because a fixture never needs a credential to prove a code path.

  NO LIVE HiveMQ BROKER WAS RUN to produce this file.
-->
<file-rbac>
    <users>
        <user>
            <name>CORP\jdoe</name>
            <password>not-a-real-hash</password>
            <roles>
                <id>ops</id>
            </roles>
        </user>
        <user>
            <!-- Not a 4.6.16 element. It was reported and the rules were still written
                 LIVE for this user until 2026-08-15, which is a switched-off account
                 being granted access by the conversion — the same fail-open class as a
                 disabled EMQX listener becoming a live bind. The grant must now come out
                 COMMENTED OUT, and the re-enrolment command with it. -->
            <name>CORP\retired</name>
            <password>not-a-real-hash</password>
            <enabled>false</enabled>
            <roles>
                <id>ops</id>
            </roles>
        </user>
        <user>
            <name>svc"quote</name>
            <password>not-a-real-hash</password>
            <roles>
                <id>ops</id>
            </roles>
        </user>
    </users>
    <roles>
        <role>
            <id>ops</id>
            <permissions>
                <permission>
                    <topic>sites/${{username}}/#</topic>
                </permission>
                <permission>
                    <topic>odd"topic/#</topic>
                    <activity>PUBLISH</activity>
                </permission>
            </permissions>
        </role>
    </roles>
    <!-- An entire section this converter has never seen. -->
    <extra-policy-section>
        <deny-topic>secret/#</deny-topic>
    </extra-policy-section>
</file-rbac>
